---
// Shared mechanism section. Identical on every case study page and the index.
// Copy anchors the ~95% show rate against the ~50% industry baseline and
// attributes it to the deposit-at-booking model plus the seven-day follow-up.
---

<section class="px-6 py-24 md:px-12">
	<div class="reveal mx-auto max-w-3xl">
		<h2 class="font-display text-[clamp(28px,3.5vw,44px)] font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-white">
			Why the bookings actually show up
		</h2>
		<div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-base leading-[1.7] text-white/70 md:text-lg">
			<p>
				Most clinics run about a 50% show rate. Half the calendar walks. Our clients run
				around 95%. Two things drive it.
			</p>
			<p>
				We collect a deposit at booking, so every appointment has money attached before the
				door opens. Then a seven day follow up system keeps the appointment in front of the
				client until they arrive.
			</p>
			<p class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-white md:text-xl">
				Deposit plus follow up. That is why the calendar holds instead of leaking.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
